1. Script to check even or odd.
This script uses the modulo operator (%) to check if the remainder when divided by 2 is 0.
read -p "Enter number: " n
if (( n % 2 == 0 )); then
    echo "$n is even"
else
    echo "$n is odd"
fi


2. Difference between if and case.

The if statement is used for evaluating general conditional expressions (e.g., comparison of variables, testing file status). The case statement is used for checking if a single value matches one of a predetermined set of patterns, making it cleaner for multi-way branching.

3. Find largest of three numbers.

read -p "Enter A: " a
read -p "Enter B: " b
read -p "Enter C: " c

# Assume A is the largest initially
largest=$a

# Check if B is greater
if (( b > largest )); then
    largest=$b
fi

# Check if C is greater
if (( c > largest )); then
    largest=$c
fi

echo "The largest number is: $largest"


