5.Loop through files in directory.
The * wildcard matches all files and directories in the current working directory, which the for loop then iterates over.
for file_name in *; do
    echo "Processing file: $file_name"
done


6.Difference between while and until.

A while loop executes its command block repeatedly as long as its controlling condition is true. An until loop executes its command block repeatedly until its controlling condition becomes true.

7.Countdown timer script.
read -p "Start countdown from: " t
while (( t > 0 )); do
    echo "$t"
    sleep 1   # Pause for 1 second
    ((t--))   # Decrement t
done
echo "Time's up!"


8.Use of break and continue.
break: Immediately terminates the execution of the entire loop (for, while, or until) and transfers control to the command immediately following the loop.
continue: Skips the remaining commands in the current iteration of the loop and starts the next iteration.

